I'd been trying the protection racket, just for a change found Dwarven
archaeologist did well. Archaeologist of course had the advantage of
IDing gems to sell for more money, and Dwarves probably have the least
enemies to worry about in the mines, since Hobbit are peaceful as well
as Gnomes and Dwarves.

I had a couple false starts, but this time I made it down to Minetown
and bought several levels of protection. And just as I was thinking
"Alright, this guy's doing good", I found a wand of wishing. I guess
that pretty much says it all. I don't wish for artifacts often, but
since I didn't really have a decent weapon I went ahead and got
Grayswandir.

I guess I was pretty lucky in general, I found an unusual abundance of
magic markers, including two in Orcus Town, one with 99 changes and
one with ~70. I tried the trick of using Asmodious as a guide, but
didn't really find it very helpful.

I found quite a lot of "oLS too. Speaking of which I had one very
embarrassing incident. Somewhere in hell I suffered what I can only
assume was YASD while wearing one and didn't even notice until later.

Still, I made it. This is my fourth.

Shortly before heading to the End Game I got a free wish from a smoky
potion. Not knowing what else to do with it I did the b(oArchon wish.
Those guys are awesome. I might have to try that with a low character
some time, in spite of the risk involved.

All the Elemental Planes were pretty easy. Very close portal on Earth
and Fire, and no real trouble on the other two either. I used jumping
boots & /oTele on Astral which worked nicely. Found the altar on the
second try.

